"""Poll Kismet's local API and keep three de-duplicated device logs.

  access_points.sqlite    Wi-Fi APs / ad-hoc / WDS (anything broadcasting a network)
  wifi_clients.sqlite     Wi-Fi client devices (phones, laptops, IoT, probing or connected)
  law_enforcement.sqlite  Body cams, in-car routers and other LE gear (Wi-Fi + Bluetooth)

One row per MAC. first_seen is the earliest observation; last_seen is a date
and only changes when the day changes, so a device seen all day costs one write.

Archimet additions (schemas of the three files above are unchanged):

  - Classification comes from one rules file (/usr/local/share/archimet/le_rules.json),
    shared with the Kismet plugin. match_reason starts with
      "Hardware: "  a device-class MAC block (see the rules file),
      "Operator: "  an operator's "Mark as LE" (note, time and source kept),
      "Learned: "   a Kismet association record linking the device to a
                    confirmed (Hardware/Operator) LE device. One hop only.
  - Anything weaker (fleet vendor, model or agency name, probes, adjacent MAC)
    goes to Review in archimet_review.sqlite, never to the LE log.
  - A small authenticated HTTP API on :2502 serves state to the plugin and
    accepts "Mark as LE" / "Unmark". It checks the caller's Kismet login.
  - Polls every 5 s with a slim field list; nothing is written when nothing changed.

  --import-inventory PATH   one-time import of the old ChatGPT inventory.db
  --migrate                 move keyword-only LE rows to Review (run once, with a backup)
  --rollback-migration      undo --migrate from its own log
"""
